# No client engines

## Forbidden

- Reintroducing `utils/bracketEngine/generation`, `scoring`, `sim`, or equivalent client generate/score engines.
- Client-side standings engines that duplicate backend High Game / Eliminator services.
- Client lane placement/movement engines — lane SSOT is backend; see `lane-ui-backend-ssot.mdc`.
- Keeping process/calculate API wrappers after live standings ship.

## Allowed

- Presentation adapters (diagram props, display name maps).
- Conflicts/UI helpers that do not own pot generation.
- Pure selected-game UX validation with **parity tests** that mirrors backend config rules — not a second SSOT for winners.

## Backend is SSOT

Preview/generate/score/standings come from API. If the backend is wrong, fix the backend — do not shadow it on the client.
